          "FAQ - Vertex Suite RCS Platform",
          "What is RCS messaging?",
          "RCS (Rich Communication Services) is the next generation of SMS that enables businesses to send rich, interactive messages directly to a user’s native messaging app. Unlike traditional SMS, RCS supports images, videos, suggested replies, carousels, and branded messaging experiences.",
          "________________________________________",
          "How is RCS different from SMS?",
          "Traditional SMS is limited to plain text messages, while RCS enables rich media content and interactive messaging features. Businesses can send images, product cards, buttons, and suggested replies through RCS, creating a more engaging customer communication experience.",
          "________________________________________",
          "Do customers need to install an app to receive RCS messages?",
          "No. RCS messages are delivered directly inside the default messaging application on supported Android devices. Customers do not need to download a separate application to interact with RCS messages.",
          "________________________________________",
          "Does RCS messaging require internet connectivity?",
          "Yes. RCS messages are delivered over mobile data or Wi-Fi. If the recipient’s device or network does not support RCS or does not have internet connectivity, the message automatically falls back to SMS to ensure delivery.",
          "________________________________________",
          "Can businesses send promotional campaigns using RCS?",
          "Yes. Businesses commonly use RCS messaging for marketing campaigns, product promotions, appointment reminders, order updates, and customer support interactions. Rich media and interactive elements help increase engagement compared to traditional SMS.",
